1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,970
This road goes straight across the Everglades!

2
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:08,728
Alligators sunning right next to the path.

3
00:00:08,728 --> 00:00:11,420
Boat rides into the Ten Thousand Islands.

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,930
And sunset on the Gulf!

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:20,053
This is the Tamiami Trail: about 110 miles from Miami, across the Everglades, to Naples.

6
00:00:20,053 --> 00:00:23,700
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:25,726
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:25,726 --> 00:00:32,650
We start in Little Havana, then Shark Valley, Big Cypress and Everglades City, and we finish in Naples!

9
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,953
We're starting in Little Havana, on Calle Ocho!

10
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:45,300
Grab a Cuban coffee and watch the domino games at Domino Park, because this street is the start of the Tamiami Trail.

11
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:50,946
West on the Tamiami Trail, and the city just stops.

12
00:00:50,946 --> 00:00:55,090
Suddenly it's sawgrass as far as you can see!

13
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,792
Welcome to Shark Valley, in Everglades National Park!

14
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:03,261
Ride the tram or rent a bike on the 15-mile loop.

15
00:01:03,261 --> 00:01:11,260
Alligators sun themselves right next to the path, and the tower halfway around looks out over the River of Grass!

16
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:17,550
Past the Miccosukee village, the sawgrass turns to cypress swamp.

17
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:19,440
Welcome to Big Cypress!

18
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:23,432
This is Big Cypress National Preserve!

19
00:01:23,432 --> 00:01:27,756
At the Oasis Visitor Center, look down into the canal.

20
00:01:27,756 --> 00:01:29,517
Alligators everywhere!

21
00:01:29,517 --> 00:01:33,600
And this swamp is home to the rare Florida panther.

22
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:40,360
Past Ochopee, home of the smallest post office in America, then south to Everglades City!

23
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:43,201
Welcome to Everglades City!

24
00:01:43,201 --> 00:01:48,946
Take a boat out into the Ten Thousand Islands and watch for dolphins and manatees.

25
00:01:48,946 --> 00:01:51,678
Then crack into fresh stone crab claws.

26
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:54,130
They're in season from mid-October!

27
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,910
Back on the Tamiami Trail, northwest to the Gulf coast!

28
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:02,675
We made it to Naples, on the Gulf!

29
00:02:02,675 --> 00:02:10,457
Walk out on the Naples Pier, first built back in 1888, and stay for the sunset over the water.

30
00:02:10,457 --> 00:02:12,610
What a way to end the day!

31
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,201
And that's the drive!

32
00:02:15,201 --> 00:02:21,060
About 110 miles from Little Havana, across the River of Grass, to the Gulf.

33
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:25,170
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

34
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:26,940
Pause and grab a screenshot!

35
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:32,051
Thanks for riding along!

36
00:02:32,051 --> 00:02:40,850
Subscribe to Road Trip Atlas for more Florida road trips, and next time we're visiting Florida's crystal-clear springs, and the manatees!
